Scope
-----
The project MIT license applies to original material that SysAgent contributors
are entitled to license. It does not replace third-party copyrights or terms.
Fonts and dependency code retain their own licenses. Dependency versions and
license identifiers are recorded in the package-lock.json files; inspect the
actual dependency distributions and preserve their notices when redistributing
a build. This file covers React, React DOM, Lucide, the bundled Noto Sans SC
fonts and the native components discussed below, not every possible build-tool
or native dependency. Current release: SysAgent 0.2.18; AgentSight 0.16.0
(unchanged).

The source export excludes reference demo HTML, extracted reference bundles,
unrelated archives, installed node_modules, validation data and the AgentSight
build cache. The official GX DEB described below is an included build input. Generated release packages are kept in Git-ignored release directories.

Prebuilt Linux x64 SysAK and AgentSight inputs and an official unmodified GX
0.6.5-2 DEB are included under vendor/ for redistribution. There are 30 vendor
input files: 25 SysAK, 3 AgentSight and 2 GX (the DEB and its manifest).
Build scripts stage and validate prebuilt inputs; they compile SysAgent code,
not SysAK, AgentSight, GX or the complete upstream coolbpf source tree.
The maintainer's binary redistribution authorization, including the user's
explicit authorization for public GX redistribution, does not replace upstream
copyrights, licenses or notices and is not a new upstream license grant.
The project MIT license does not relicense those native components.

Retained UI, data and styles include material ported from a reference demo.
The permission record for that reference and its derivatives has not been
established by this review. Excluding extracted bundles does not establish
rights in retained derivatives; confirm them before publishing the source.

SysAK remains an external native dependency. Its local build provenance and
component license inventory must be established before distributing a native
bundle. Do not assume the top-level SysAgent MIT license covers SysAK.

AgentSight remains an external service. Inspected sources include Apache-2.0
project code, LGPL-2.1 OR BSD-2-Clause eBPF sources, and a separate GPL-2.0-only
source file whose inclusion in the release binary was not established.
Embedded eBPF objects declare GPL; that marker alone does not establish a
GPL-only source license. Determine the applicable redistribution route,
preserve its notices and fulfill any corresponding-source obligations before
distributing the runtime. The source/build cache is not included here.

The inspected AppImage also bundles desktop libraries without a complete
per-library license inventory. Establish their terms and satisfy applicable
notice and source obligations, including LGPL requirements where applicable.
Native binaries retain local build-path references that require review.

GX 0.6.5-2 and scoped coolbpf changes
------------------------------------
Redistributed file: vendor/gx/linux-x64/gx_0.6.5-2_amd64.deb
SHA-256: a471bf61863c61744b102ba19a8620feea68d9aeaab8591c9d056f3cbe5b1902
This is the official unchanged upstream DEB from the SysAK AI build input.
Inspected DEB metadata identifies package gx, version 0.6.5-2, architecture
amd64 and maintainer alibaba-cloud. The DEB is verified and copied unchanged
into the release; signed retrieval URLs and parameters are not distributed.

The inspected GX RPM metadata lists the license strings literally as
"LBPLv2+" and "MIT". Do not silently normalize "LBPLv2+" or treat this metadata
as proof that the whole DEB is MIT-licensed. The inspected DEB lacks a complete
copyright/license file. That absence does not establish a proprietary license,
and neither SysAgent's MIT license nor the user's redistribution authorization
relicenses GX or upstream source code. Preserve upstream copyrights and terms;
confirm applicable notices and any corresponding-source obligations from the
actual upstream licenses. Unchanged redistribution does not remove them.

scripts/coolbpf-gx-0.6.5-2.patch contains scoped upstream coolbpf changes for
GX version/configured-state checks and verified package caching and hashes.
It is credential-free and contains no signed URLs. It does not modify the
official GX DEB. The full upstream source tree is not vendored; this patch is
not a complete corresponding-source delivery. Upstream source files retain
their own licenses, not a blanket SysAgent MIT relicense. The root build uses
prebuilt inputs rather than applying this patch for a complete upstream rebuild.

The main SysAgent DEB exactly depends on gx (= 0.6.5-2) and
sysom-agentsight-runtime (= 0.16.0). The offline installer installs three local
DEBs: GX first, then AgentSight runtime, then SysAgent. The installation-only
root helper checks the configured GX version and required GX files, creates
/etc/ld.so.conf.d/sysagent-gx.conf containing /usr/lib64 followed by a newline,
and runs ldconfig. /usr/share/gx/lib is the GX executable's RPATH, not a global
loader path. GUI startup never downloads or elevates. Successful package and
loader setup does not prove hardware/driver-dependent GPU tracing; that
capability has not been established here.

